<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.4.5: Perfect Square and Squared Factors</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02383</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.4.5: Perfect Square and Squared Factors</md:title>
    <md:uuid>f51e3e7f-01c3-4a9f-974c-0467bd4d5ba1</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>
<title>Student Activity </title>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Answer the following questions for expression \(4x^2−28x+c\).</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Find the value of \(c\) to make the expression a perfect square.</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 49</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Write an equivalent expression in the form of squared factors.</item>
</list>
<para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Squared factors: \((2x−7)^2\).</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Solve the equation \(4x^2−28x=-33\) by completing the square. Show your reasoning.</item>
</list>
<para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> </para>
<para>\(\begin{aligned} 4 x^{2}-28 x &amp;=-33 \\ 4 x^{2}-28 x+49 &amp;=-33+49 \\ (2 x-7)^{2} &amp;=16 \\ \sqrt{(2 x-7)^{2}} &amp;=\sqrt{16} \\ 2 x-7 &amp;=4 \\ 2 x-7 &amp;=-4 \\ 2 x &amp;=11 \\ 2 x &amp;=3 \end{aligned}\)</para>
<para class="os-raise-noindent"> \(x=\frac{11}{2} \text { and } x=\frac{3}{2}\) </para>
<title>Response to Student Thinking</title>
<title>Points to Emphasize</title>
<para>If students struggle with completing the square, use the activity Lesson 9.5.3 to highlight key ideas on the completing the square process based on student work in the cool down.</para></section>
</content>
